# Machine-local agent config, written by Connect (apps/gui/src/main/providers.ts).
# `.mcp.json` (Claude Code's own project-scope file, written by `claude mcp add
# -s project`), `.codex/config.toml` (codex), `.grok/config.toml` (grok) and
# `opencode.json` (opencode) each hardcode absolute paths to this machine's
# Kanmer install and board worktree via the shared Invocation shape —
# committing one would be as inert to anyone else as a checked-in `.mcp.json`
# pointing at someone else's machine. `.claude/skills/`, `.opencode/skills/`,
# `.grok/skills/` is a legacy local copy of the plugin skills (the canonical
# ones are plugins/kanmer/skills/). Antigravity now owns skills/MCP in its user
# plugin; its old `.agents` paths are migration inputs, not active writers.
# Keep those paths ignored while a reconnect has not yet retired residue from
# an older checkout; they are machine-local state, never source files.
# Note `.agents/plugins/marketplace.json` is NOT here — it's a real repo file,
# not a Connect-written artifact, so `.agents/` itself is never blanket-ignored.
# All of the below are untracked deliberately — and `scripts/release.mjs`
# counts untracked files as a dirty tree, so leaving them here blocks every
# release. Every `copySkills` destination in providers.ts is checked against
# this file by a test in apps/gui/src/main/providers.test.ts.
.mcp.json
.codex/config.toml
.grok/config.toml
opencode.json
.claude/skills/
.opencode/skills/
.grok/skills/
.agents/mcp_config.json
.agents/skills/
